== Checks
look.py (plain Python routing, written separately) on A_bed_600000.bin gives threads 3.938 wet 0.5093 rough 3.0160 maxshare 0.1600: the same as the C line at 600000. Water per row is 64.000000 in every row.
Start of A: rough 0.864 against 3/sqrt(12) = 0.866 expected of the noise.
Rounding: writing q*w/sum as w*(q/sum), or compiling -O2 against -O3 -march=native, changed rough at 5,000 steps from 0.704 to 0.719 / 0.714 (same seed): single runs are not reproducible past the last bit, only their statistics.

== What I had to decide
1. 'rough ... mean over those cells': taken as all cells of rows 64..191 (the wet-cells-only reading is the extra column).
2. A stream with s <= 0 that still gets water (the no-downhill case) carries sand if s + Cs > 0; a stream with no water carries none.
3. Row 0 sends sand into row 1 and row 254 into row 255, though rows 0 and 255 never change; the greatest |dh| includes the sideways moves; measures at step t use the bed after t steps.
